Adds a **new UI template** to `apps/ecommerce/cordelia` from a **Figma kit** —
every storefront surface rendered in the new pack over the **unchanged** shared
`domain`/`data`/`bloc` layers. `dailymart` is the proven exemplar; `grofast`
was the first built by this recipe.

**Read `docs/how-to/add-storefront-template.md` and follow every phase.** It is
the canonical version of this rule and carries the detail Cursor cannot inline.
Also read the pack spec sheets in `docs/ai-rules/style-packs/` — an existing
one as a model, and `_TEMPLATE.md` as the form to fill.

## The six phases

0. **Inputs** — Figma file key, lowercase template id, licence note. No Figma
   access, no skill; never hand-transcribe from screenshots.
1. **Kit → contracts** — sample **real screens** (never the kit's foundation
   page, which lies). Produce the theme preset (light + dark), the theme config
   JSON, the pack const files under `lib/templates/<id>/constants/`, and the
   spec sheet §0–§9 **before any screen exists**. Type scale comes from the
   kit, not from Material defaults.
2. **Frame inventory** — bucket every frame: direct match → build from it;
   supported surface with **no frame** → compose from the pack's own recipes,
   never skip; frame with **no feature** behind it → discard and record the
   deviation. Auth/splash/onboarding/discovery are shared chrome, never
   templated. Confirm buckets and the tab set with the user before coding.
3. **Implement** — register the template (enum + `wireValue`, `StorefrontPage`
   switch, a branch in **every** `StorefrontTemplateSwitch`), build the pack kit
   to the roster, then per-feature `presentation/templates/<id>/` slices. Reuse
   before you build — but only what already exists; don't invent a shared
   abstraction on the first pass. Duplication is expected here and Phase 5
   is where it resolves. Bottom inset on **every** state branch, exhaustive
   switches, `ValueConst`-only copy, skeletons that mirror the loaded
   structure — never a spinner.
4. **Prove it with tests, not a device** — ship tests in the same commit.
   Manual fakes only, no network, `bloc_test` `MockBloc`. A pack owes: template
   dispatch + no cross-pack fall-through, warm revisit with no skeleton,
   session teardown, long-label wrapping, stock states, signed-out browse +
   gated taps, an error branch whose retry re-dispatches, and empty ≠ error.
5. **Review & promotion** — `/review-code`, then promote duplicates by scope
   (core + gallery entry / `Cordelia*` / feature mixin / pack kit), re-running
   the tests after each promotion. Contract audit: every spec-sheet row must
   have a call site.
6. **Document** — finish the spec sheet through §15, add the `design.md` §1
   catalog row, update the progress docs.

## Inherited, never rebuilt

Warm-start caching (`BlocCache`/`ScopedBlocCache`), failures mapped to copy
once at the presentation boundary (never `e.toString()`; react to
`Failure.refused`'s `code`, not its message), `CrashReporterService`
(registered in `main.dart`, static singleton, no-op on web and debug), and
notifications (real per-store data — the pack maps `NotificationKind` to its
own glyphs and owns nothing else).

## States the kit will not draw for you

No UI kit contains these; all three packs compose them from recipes they
already own, and two are store-policy failures rather than gaps:

- **Stock and availability** — sold-out mark + disabled add control, photo at
  `kSoldOutImageOpacity`, quantity capped at `purchaseLimit`, cart line
  labelled from `CartItemAvailabilityX`.
- **Delivery fee** — in **all three** totals panels (cart, checkout, track
  order); a panel that omits it shows a total the shopper is not charged.
- **Report a review / block its author** — App Store Guideline 1.2 for any app
  with user-generated content. One sheet does both.
- **Signed-out** — browsing needs no account; every *write*-shaped tap goes
  through `context.requireSignIn()`, which **pushes** Login. `ProfileSignedOut`
  must render, or a guest's Profile shimmers forever.
